From 99d895c570abb25f6a506b0acc6a09d49d1c0b75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO Phase II executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 20:47:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase II checkpoint: per-product weight field (default 1.0),
 RHS + Jacobian

Add REACTION_PRODUCT_WEIGHTS(MAX_COMPOUNDS, nb_reactions), default 1.0, applied
to every product (gain) deposit in get_temporal_derivatives and get_jacobian.
Reactant depletion (loss) is never weighted. This is the encoding decided in the
design thread: one reaction per unordered pair, gain split by weights, loss once;
M_ijk rides on the weight, K_ij (and the diagonal 1/2) on the rate.

get_jacobian is a separate code path from the RHS, so the weight is applied there
explicitly (30 product deposits across the 1-/2-/3-body reactant branches) to
match the RHS -- a weight in the RHS but not the Jacobian would give correct
derivative values with a wrong Jacobian and degrade Newton silently.

No coagulation reactions generated yet. With weight = 1.0 everywhere, the 0D
2-grain reference case is byte-identical (abundances.out + dust_distribution.out,
-O0) to the pre-change binary, i.e. still bit-identical to nmgc-2.0. This isolates
'did the field perturb anything' (no) from 'did coagulation perturb anything'.
